{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: lane G, the checkers. Implement the Checker base and the isolated check runner, with a tests checker, a types checker and an LLM reviewer, so obligations are fulfilled by signed check acts from authorized checker identities.","body":{"conditions":"(1) The contract's Checker base class and runner wrapper, implemented: a checker service (Worker) holding its delegation key outside any sandbox, receiving check jobs bound to (lane, generation, integration commit or filtered snapshot, checker configuration hash, runner digest), and signing check acts per R-EXEC and R-CARRY. (2) An isolated runner in a separate Sandbox container from the publisher: read-only access only, no canonical write token or remote, no signing keys, fetch the exact pinned integration and verify HEAD before running; the default whole-tree input, and scoped inputs delivered as a filtered snapshot in an isolated workspace with attempted access to excluded data tested; argument-array exec with exit codes checked (npm ci before npm test). (3) Three checkers: tests (npm test), types (tsc --noEmit), and an LLM reviewer that posts a note and an advisory check with findings (Workers AI or the Anthropic API, with the key held by the checker service only), each clearly labelled machine-run. (4) Tests: unit tests for job binding and signing; live runs against a small Artifacts repo in gitseq-spike showing pass, fail, a changed test with unchanged source rerunning, a scoped checker unable to read an excluded file, and a runner that cannot push; cold and warm timings recorded in a dated note. (5) README in plain English per ISO 24495-1.","target_head":"ca61351fc3a886760b2b7d1d11e241a05b38550e","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}